# crucible-asic-starter

A student reference workspace for serial protocols and open-source ASIC flows.

I2C, SPI, UART, low-speed USB and 10 Mbit Ethernet now have pinned upstream RTL, self-checking simulations with
deliberate failure controls, SG13G2 mapped synthesis, routed DEF/SPEF, typical
and slow extracted timing, and independently decoded GDS. These are fixed-function
reference blocks, **not a Tiny Tapeout submission** and not a general-purpose
reprogrammable protocol emulator.

Jane Street requires a programmable emulator on its IHP CMOS5L template.
The standalone SG13G2 builds do not establish competition compliance.
See the [official requirements](https://blog.janestreet.com/protocol-emulator-asic-competition/).

## Run a reference block in WSL

In an interactive login Bash shell, from this repository:

```sh
igny init
unset CRUCIBLE_ENV
cd hw/protocols/i2c
make lint sim
make flow
node verify_build.mjs all
```

Repeat in the existing SPI, UART, stretch/usb_ls and stretch/ethernet directories.
USB uses a 12 MHz reference core clock; Ethernet uses external 2.5 MHz MII clocks.
On another machine, use
igny workspace sync from each unit and supply the matching PDK through
IHP_PDK_ROOT. Source revisions, versions, commands and coverage are in:

- [I2C reference build](hw/protocols/i2c/README.md)
- [SPI reference build](hw/protocols/spi/README.md)
- [UART reference build](hw/protocols/uart/README.md)
- [Low-speed USB reference build](hw/protocols/stretch/usb_ls/README.md)
- [10 Mbit Ethernet reference build](hw/protocols/stretch/ethernet/README.md)

## Student decks

Each current deck has 44 slides with worked waveform decodes, numerical examples,
actual RTL walkthroughs, guided labs and answers, sourced lecture notes, measured
results and explicit verification limits, using the supplied APB video identity.
The links below are the current revision. Superseded versions have been moved to
the recoverable cleanup archive; v2 was rejected by the human as too basic and
is not the current lesson.

- [I2C lesson](docs/student_decks/I2C_Protocol_Students_Ignytion_VIDEO.pptx)
- [SPI lesson](docs/student_decks/SPI_Protocol_Students_Ignytion_VIDEO.pptx)
- [UART lesson](docs/student_decks/UART_Protocol_Students_Ignytion_VIDEO.pptx)

These three stable lesson files are the verified 44-slide v11 packages. Their
current validation receipts, curriculum manifests and reviewed renders remain
in docs/.deck_build. Duplicate version-named files are no longer student entry points.

## Protocol whitepapers

Each current paper has 24 A4 pages adapted to the supplied APB primer, covering
protocol rules, worked calculations, actual RTL boundaries, directed verification,
the implementation stages, measured SG13G2 results, reproduction and glossaries.
PPTX text/tables and the first three measured-waveform charts remain editable;
the PDFs are searchable. Package/content and live-evidence checks passed.
The revised papers' complete final-page visual acceptance remains unfinished.

| Protocol | Editable A4 source | Searchable PDF |
| --- | --- | --- |
| I2C | [PPTX](docs/I2C_Protocol_RTL_to_GDS_Ignytion_A4.pptx) | [PDF](docs/I2C_Protocol_RTL_to_GDS_Ignytion_A4.pdf) |
| SPI | [PPTX](docs/SPI_Protocol_RTL_to_GDS_Ignytion_A4.pptx) | [PDF](docs/SPI_Protocol_RTL_to_GDS_Ignytion_A4.pdf) |
| UART | [PPTX](docs/UART_Protocol_RTL_to_GDS_Ignytion_A4.pptx) | [PDF](docs/UART_Protocol_RTL_to_GDS_Ignytion_A4.pdf) |
| Low-speed USB | [PPTX](docs/USB_LS_Protocol_RTL_to_GDS_Ignytion_A4.pptx) | [PDF](docs/USB_LS_Protocol_RTL_to_GDS_Ignytion_A4.pdf) |
| 10 Mbit Ethernet | [PPTX](docs/Ethernet_10M_Protocol_RTL_to_GDS_Ignytion_A4.pptx) | [PDF](docs/Ethernet_10M_Protocol_RTL_to_GDS_Ignytion_A4.pdf) |

Authoring scripts, acceptance ledgers and preview evidence are in the private
recovery archive described below, not the deliverables folder. USB and Ethernet
papers use labelled ideal
examples, not invented measured VCD plots. Ethernet's current SDC does not group
the MII clocks asynchronously; its reported slacks are reference timing results,
not arbitrary external-PHY clock-domain or reset signoff.

## Layout and remaining scope

- specs/: supplied PDFs; the Ethernet PDF is a PHY datasheet, not IEEE 802.3.
- hw/protocols/i2c, spi, uart: implemented reference blocks and numbered stages.
- hw/protocols/stretch/usb_ls, ethernet: confirmed low-speed USB and 10 Mbit
  Ethernet reference builds with passing directed tests and decoded routed GDS.
  USB is a restricted HID-host engine with unchecked receive CRC and incomplete
  PID validation; full enumeration and USB compliance are not proven. Ethernet
  is a full-duplex digital MAC requiring an external analog PHY, not a transceiver.
- hw/core and tapeout/: integrated emulator and submission scaffold, not
  implemented or release-qualified by these standalone builds.
- .context.md: append-only progress and actual Claude collaboration.
- hw/protocols/i2c/GATES.md: combined reference-build and lesson acceptance ledger.

All five reference-unit stage recipes are implemented. DFT and foundry physical
verification deliberately fail instead of reporting placeholder success.
Foundry DRC/LVS, antenna and full-chip signoff have **not been performed**.
Empty router DRC reports and GDS/DEF agreement are limited implementation/export
checks, not manufacturability proof.

Generated binary and standard-format outputs retain native formats. Source
files retain integration headers and original upstream notices; adjacent
README and validation receipts record generated-artifact provenance. Upstream
ownership is not replaced by the Ignytion integration header.

Not affiliated with or endorsed by Jane Street. Jane Street is a trademark of
Jane Street Group, LLC.

## Cleanup and recovery

The visible docs folder contains only the five current PPTX/PDF pairs, challenge
requirements and the three canonical student decks. Authoring/inspection/export
scripts, agent gate files, .deck_build, chart scratch and hidden agent state are
removed from the visible workspace. Compiled simulation executables and non-final
floorplan/placement/CTS databases are also removed. RTL, testbenches, licences,
Makefiles, source VCDs, decisive logs, mapped netlists, final routed DEF/ODB/SPEF,
GDS and timing reports remain in their project locations.

Everything removed is recoverable outside Janes_street at:
`C:\Users\ignyt\AppData\Local\Ignytion\CleanupArchives\janes-street-20261005`.
Its `manifest.json` records original workspace-relative paths and SHA256 hashes;
archived data lives beneath `workspace/`. The earlier cleanup archives now live
under `workspace/.unlazy/` there, not in the current workspace.

To restore, use the recorded original relative path only when the destination
is absent; never overwrite newer work. Restore the required authoring inputs and
their original evidence paths before rerunning archived document tooling.
No final document, RTL or GDS bytes were changed by cleanup. No permanent deletion
or external publication occurred. The archive's GATES.md and cleanup.ps1 hold
the cleanup verification receipt and read-only recovery/preservation checks.
